This is a baseline simulation setup to test the impedance simulator.
    ngtest.c() provides function definitions to run a spice simulation and retrieve values
    a lot of these functions are at least partially created by chat so use at your own risk
    ngtest.c() provides the following function definitions:

        config(): runs spice sim for an RL circuit and saves results to the global vectors, might add argument parsing 
        to make switching between simulated circuits easier, but right now it just runs one hard-coded one

        print(): prints the saved data vectors + current to a text file

        get_VL(time): returns voltage across the inductor at given time in seconds 

        double get_vin(time): returns input voltage at given time in seconds 

        double get_current(time): returns current through the inductor (through system in this case) at 
        given time in microseconds

    difeq.c provides a function (iterate_difeq) definition for an iteratable approximation for the differential equation for an RL circuit
    this serves as a proof of concept for something that can be translated into RTL

    run_test.c: provides a main function that iterates the differential equation function and compares values to the 
    values from the spice sim.  
